fix(pip): Review of the stable overlay fix: no stale facts, and the same blind spot in the boost

Reviewing the previous commit (the withheld lens optic case) found two things.

One, the new clause could latch. The optic facts it reads (svp_optic_magnifies, svp_lens_fov) are
published only from CWeapon::UpdateSecondVP, which returns early unless the weapon is the active
item, so after the player puts a scoped weapon away they keep their last values. A predicate built
on them alone would stay true from then on, keeping the upscaler in its spatial-only mode - a
quality regression rather than a crash, and a silent one. The clause is now gated on the ADS
progress from the game, which is refreshed every frame and is zero when nothing is aimed, so it can
only fire while an optic is actually up.

Two, the same blind spot exists one function away, and it is the cause of the pixelated screen the
player reported earlier. ScopeResolutionRequested() decides whether to raise the upscaler's internal
resolution while an optic is in use, and it also looked at the zoom factor - at or below 1 for this
pack's optics - or at IsSVPActive(), which is false for the sights that keep the 3DSS path. A
thermal sight therefore never raised the resolution, and its screen, which is the whole image for
that optic, was reconstructed from the upscaler's internal size. It now also triggers on the optic
facts, so screen type sights get the same treatment as the rest.

Note for a later round: the stale facts are a latent issue beyond these two predicates. The
evaluated state feeds svp_make_inputs from the same values, so a holstered scoped weapon can keep
the lens set alive and the state true. That is not introduced here and is left alone rather than
changed mid stream.